Creating a digital literacy quiz in Google Forms is an effective way to assess foundational computer and online skills. A well-structured quiz typically covers areas such as internet safety, information searching, and basic digital tool proficiency
. 
Here is a guide on how to structure, create, and populate a digital literacy quiz in Google Forms.
1. Planning Your Digital Literacy Quiz :
·	Target Audience: Define if this is for beginners, students, or professionals.
·	Key Topics: Select from areas like computer basics, internet safety (cybersecurity), searching, and communication (email/netiquette).
·	Quiz Goal: Is this for evaluation, or for a "self-assessment" to help them learn? 
2. Setting Up the Google Form :
1.	Open Google Forms: Go to forms.google.com and select "Blank Quiz" to start with scoring enabled.
2.	Turn on Quiz Mode: Go to Settings > Click Make this a quiz.
3.	Quiz Title & Description: Title it "Digital Literacy Quiz" and add a description like: "Test your skills in staying safe online and using digital tools."
4.	Add Questions: Use a mix of multiple-choice, checkboxes, or short-answer questions.
5.	Set Answers: For each question, click Answer key to assign points and select the correct answer(s). 
